  {
    "episode_id": 88436,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/8/88436.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 8,
    "turn_text": "I don't think he's inclined to be that guy, Mark. Kevin McCarthy's been in leadership here 14 years. I've watched a video when he was in Bakersfield in 2011, had been in leadership a couple of years then, and said he had the same three threats to America that he says now. First one was the accumulation of indebted, and he hasn't made any progress in delivering on that promise in that period of time. It's causing me to question whether that's the main thing that's in his heart. If he really wants to deliver on those promises to the American people, or he's captured by this town, this Pelosi-style operation of Congress that serves lobbyists and interests in Washington. And I believe that it is essential that we restore this Congress to its operation on behalf of the American people.",
