    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/8/88436.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 10,
    "turn_text": "Well, I mean, the hard part is to construct a set of rules. See, every rule up here can be weighed, Mark. That's why we have these omnibus bills like the $1.7 trillion that the 18th Senate Republican senators just voted for a couple of weeks ago and ran or ran through. So we've got new rules. We've gone back to some rules so we've negotiated so far. But those rules can be waived too. We've got to construct something that's sufficient to align Mr. McCarthy's interest with the interest of the American people. So we're going to work really hard at that. We have been working incessantly for the last two months at that. And if you can do it and we can get there, then I don't know that there's nothing. I don't have any animus against Kevin McCarthy. But we are going to get that done.",
